{"book":24,"chapter":40,"context":{"chapter":40,"title":"Gedaliah at Mizpah","summary":"The Babylonian commander frees Jeremiah from a line of chained captives at Ramah and lets him choose where to live; Jeremiah joins the new governor, Gedaliah, at Mizpah. Scattered Judeans return and gather a rich harvest, but Gedaliah refuses to believe a warning that Ishmael plans to kill him.","background":"Mizpah, a few miles north of Jerusalem, became Judah's administrative center after Jerusalem's destruction. Gedaliah came from the family of Shaphan, officials who had protected Jeremiah (26:24). A seal impression found at Lachish reads 'belonging to Gedalyahu, who is over the house,' possibly the same man in an earlier royal post.","customs":[{"term":"Wine and summer fruits","verses":"40:10-12","note":"Grapes, figs and other late-summer produce were pressed or dried and stored in jars for the winter."}],"watchFor":["A Babylonian officer explains God's judgment to Jeremiah (vv. 2–3).","'Fear not to serve the Chaldeans' (v. 9).","Gedaliah's trust in Ishmael (v. 16)."],"connections":["2 Kings 25:22-24","Jeremiah 26:24","Jeremiah 39:14","Jeremiah 31:15"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["הַדָּבָר","hadavar","H1697","HTd/Ncmsa","the word"],["אֲשֶׁר","'asher-","H834","HTr","which"],["הָיָה","hayah","H1961","HVqp3ms","it came"],["אֶל","'el-","H413","HR","to"],["יִרְמְיָהוּ","yirmeyahu","H3414","HNpm","Jeremiah"],["מֵאֵת","me'et","H854","HR/R","from with"],["יְהוָה","yahweh","H3068","HNpt","Yahweh"],["אַחַר","'achar","H310","HAcmsc","after"],["שַׁלַּח","shalach","H7971","HVpcc","set free"],["אֹתוֹ","'oto","H853","HTo/Sp3ms","<obj.> him"],["נְבוּזַרְאֲדָן","nevuzar'adan","H5018","HNpm","Nebuzaradan"],["רַב","rav-","H7227","HNcmsc","[the] chief of"],["טַבָּחִים","tabachim","H2876","HNcmpa","[the] bodyguards"],["מִן","min-","H4480","HR","from"],["הָרָמָה","haramah","H7414","HTd/Npl","<the> Ramah"],["בְּקַחְתּוֹ","bekachto","H3947","HR/Vqcc/Sp3ms","when took he"],["אֹתוֹ","'oto","H853","HTo/Sp3ms